// title: "Release branch protection template"
// summary: "Require Tests and Release policy checks for main while preserving human control of release merges."
//
// Used when: A repository administrator reviews or deliberately changes protection for the main release branch after the required workflows exist on the default dev branch; cloning this repository, committing this file, or running CI does not apply these settings.
//
// Read by: The conversion command in docs/GITHUB.md runs custom-pieces/framework/scp/jsonc.py to create local/github-api/main-protection.json under custom-pieces; an administrator then supplies that strict-JSON file to the separate gh api --method PUT branches/main/protection operation.
//
// Updated by: Human maintainers edit this template when the release-branch policy, required Tests or Release policy checks, or their GitHub Actions bindings change, regenerate the disposable API payload, and inspect it before applying it to their intended repository.
//
// Affects: Only a deliberately applied API payload changes GitHub protection: the branch must be up to date, Tests and Release policy must pass, conversations must be resolved, administrator enforcement applies, and force pushes and deletion are blocked; zero approving reviews are required.
//
// Reference: docs/GITHUB.md
{
  "required_status_checks": {
    "strict": true,
    "checks": [
      {"context": "Tests", "app_id": 15368},
      {"context": "Release policy", "app_id": 15368}
    ]
  },
  "enforce_admins": true,
  "required_pull_request_reviews": {
    "required_approving_review_count": 0
  },
  "restrictions": null,
  "required_conversation_resolution": true,
  "allow_force_pushes": false,
  "allow_deletions": false
}
